2026-11-09 20:26:22 [INFO] agentic_cli: TOOL_CALL: write_file args={'content': '# Agentic CLI - Project Overview\n\n## Project Summary\n\n**Agentic CLI** is a minimal, from-scratch agentic coding tool CLI built in Python. It provides an interactive terminal interface where users can give coding tasks to an AI agent that uses tools to read, search, edit, and run code until the task is completed.\n\n- **Name**: agentic-cli\n- **Version**: 0.1.0\n- **Language**: Python 3.11+\n- **License**: MIT\n- **Repository**: `/Users/glbtech/PycharmProjects/AIAgests/backend`\n\n---\n\n## Purpose & Scope\n\n### Purpose\nCreate a lightweight, provider-agnostic CLI coding agent that:\n- Works with any OpenAI-compatible API (Ollama, OpenAI, OpenRouter, NVIDIA NIM, etc.)\n- Provides a secure, permission-gated tool execution environment\n- Supports extensible skills and agents system\n- Offers transparent reasoning and tool execution visibility\n\n### Scope\n- **In Scope**: Core agent loop, 8 built-in tools, permission system, skills/agents framework, completion verification, logging\n- **Out of Scope**: GUI, web interface, built-in model hosting, non-OpenAI-compatible providers (Anthropic, Gemini - stubbed only)\n\n---\n\n## Architecture\n\n### High-Level Architecture\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                        CLI (src/cli.py)                         │\n│  ┌─────────────┐  ┌─────────────┐  ┌─────────────────────────┐  │\n│  │ Input       │  │ Slash       │  │ Agent Loop              │  │\n│  │ Normalizer  │  │ Commands    │  │ (src/agent.py)          │  │\n│  └──────┬──────┘  └──────┬──────┘  └───────────┬─────────────┘  │\n│         │                │                     │                │\n│         ▼                ▼                     ▼                │\n│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │\n│  │              Tool Registry (src/tools/registry.py)      │   │\n│  │  ┌────────┐ ┌────────┐ ┌────────┐ ┌────────┐ ┌────────┐  │   │\n│  │  │read_   │ │write_  │ │edit_   │ │glob    │ │grep    │  │   │\n│  │  │file    │ │file    │ │file    │ │        │ │        │  │   │\n│  │  └────────┘ └────────┘ └────────┘ └────────┘ └────────┘  │   │\n│  │  ┌────────┐ ┌────────┐ ┌────────┐                          │   │\n│  │  │bash    │ │ask_    │ │plan    │                          │   │\n│  │  │        │ │user    │ │        │                          │   │\n│  │  └────────┘ └────────┘ └────────┘                          │   │\n│  └────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┘   │\n│                           │                                       │\n│         ┌─────────────────┼─────────────────┐                    │\n│         ▼                 ▼                 ▼                    │\n│  ┌────────────┐   ┌────────────┐   ┌────────────┐               │\n│  │ Permission │   │  Provider  │   │  Logger    │               │\n│  │ Gate       │   │  Adapter   │   │  (logs/)   │               │\n│  └────────────┘   └────────────┘   └────────────┘               │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### Module Structure\n\n```\nsrc/\n├── __init__.py              # Package initialization\n├── agent.py                 # Agent loop with max steps, loop detection, output limit handling\n├── agents.py                # Agent loader (individual .md files + agents.md)\n├── cli.py                   # REPL with slash commands, rich console UI\n├── completion.py            # Completion reviewer (verifies task completion)\n├── config.py                # Configuration from env/file (.env support)\n├── logger.py                # Rotating file logging (logs/log.log)\n├── permissions.py           # Path validation, deny list, permission gate\n├── provider.py              # OpenAI-compatible provider adapter\n├── skills.py                # Skill loader (.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md)\n├── system_prompt.py         # System prompt builder + AGENT.md loader\n├── types.py                 # Internal message format (provider-independent)\n└── tools/\n    ├── __init__.py          # Tool exports\n    ├── registry.py          # Tool registry\n    ├── read_file.py         # Read file with offset/limit\n    ├── write_file.py        # Write file (creates dirs, overwrites)\n    ├── edit_file.py         # Edit file by exact string replacement\n    ├── glob_tool.py         # Find files matching glob pattern\n    ├── grep_tool.py         # Regex search in files\n    ├── bash_tool.py         # Execute shell commands\n    ├── ask_tool.py          # Ask user questions (with options)\n    └── plan_tool.py         # Present plans for approval\n```\n\n---\n\n## Key Features\n\n### 1. Provider-Agnostic LLM Integration\n- Works with any OpenAI-compatible API endpoint\n- Tested with: NVIDIA NIM, Ollama, OpenAI, OpenRouter\n- Configurable via environment variables or `.env` file\n- Supports reasoning models (qwen3.5, deepseek-r1, etc.)\n\n### 2. 8 Built-in Tools\n| Tool | Category | Permission | Description |\n|------|----------|------------|-------------|\n| `read_file` | Read | Auto | Read file with optional offset/limit |\n| `write_file` | Write | Prompt | Write content, creates parent dirs |\n| `edit_file` | Write | Prompt | Exact string replacement (unique match required) |\n| `glob` | Read | Auto | Find files matching glob pattern |\n| `grep` | Read | Auto | Regex search in files |\n| `bash` | Write | Prompt | Execute shell commands (with deny list) |\n| `ask_user` | Interactive | Auto | Ask user questions with optional choices |\n| `plan` | Interactive | Auto | Present implementation plans for approval |\n\n### 3. Permission System\n- **Auto-allowed**: `read_file`, `glob`, `grep` (run automatically)\n- **Prompt required**: `write_file`, `edit_file`, `bash` (ask each time)\n- **Interactive options**: `y` (allow once), `a` (always allow), `u` (auto-allow), `n` (deny), `d` (deny always)\n- **Pre-configuration**: `/permission allow <tool> [always|auto]`\n- **Security**: Path validation (blocks outside project root), command deny list\n\n### 4. Agent Loop\n- Maximum steps per task (default: 50, configurable)\n- Loop detection (stops on repeated identical tool calls)\n- Output token limit handling with automatic continuation\n- Empty response retry with clarification callback\n- Context window utilization logging\n\n### 5. Completion Verification\n- Automatic review after agent claims completion\n- Uses separate LLM call to verify task fulfillment\n- Up to 3 attempts (configurable) with feedback loop\n- Returns detailed findings if incomplete\n\n### 6. Skills & Agents System\n- **Skills**: `.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` with YAML frontmatter\n- **Agents**: `.agents/agents/<name>.md` or `agents/agents.md`\n- Auto-discovered and loaded at startup\n- Included in system prompt for agent awareness\n- CLI commands: `/skills`, `/agents` for management\n\n### 7. Slash Commands\n| Command | Description |\n|---------|-------------|\n| `/help` | Show help |\n| `/clear` | Clear conversation history & permissions |\n| `/model [name]` | Show or change model |\n| `/permission [list|allow|deny|reset]` | Manage tool permissions |\n| `/skills [list|show|create]` | Manage skills |\n| `/agents [list|show|create]` | Manage agents |\n| `/exit` | Exit the CLI |\n\n### 8. Logging System\n- Rotating file handler (10MB, 5 backups) at `logs/log.log`\n- Logs: commands, permissions, tool calls, reasoning, errors\n- Console shows warnings/errors only\n\n### 9. Input Normalization\n- Normalizes user input to English objective + actionable tasks\n- Corrects spelling/grammar, preserves intent\n- Uses separate lightweight agent loop\n\n---\n\n## Dependencies\n\n### Runtime Dependencies (from `pyproject.toml`)\n| Package | Version | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|---------|\n| `httpx` | >=0.27 | Async HTTP client for LLM API calls |\n| `pydantic` | >=2.8 | Data validation (used in types) |\n| `python-dotenv` | >=1.0 | Load `.env` configuration files |\n| `rich` | >=13.7 | Terminal UI (panels, tables, markdown) |\n| `pyyaml` | >=6.0 | Parse YAML frontmatter in skills/agents |\n\n### Development Dependencies\n| Package | Version | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|---------|\n| `pytest` | >=8.2 | Test framework |\n| `pytest-asyncio` | >=0.23 | Async test support |\n| `ruff` | >=0.5 | Linting/formatting |\n\n### Python Version\n- **Requires**: Python >= 3.11\n- **StrEnum fallback** for Python 3.10 compatibility\n\n---\n\n## Configuration\n\n### Environment Variables\n| Variable | Default | Description |\n|----------|---------|-------------|\n| `AGENTIC_BASE_URL` | `http://localhost:11434/v1` | OpenAI-compatible API endpoint |\n| `AGENTIC_API_KEY` | `ollama` | Provider API key |\n| `AGENTIC_MODEL` | `llama3.1` | Model name |\n| `AGENTIC_PROJECT_ROOT` | `.` | Project directory |\n| `AGENTIC_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` | `300` | Model request timeout |\n| `AGENTIC_MAX_COMPLETION_TOKENS` | `8192` | Max generated tokens per response |\n| `AGENTIC_CONTEXT_WINDOW_TOKENS` | `32768` | Context budget for token tracking |\n| `AGENTIC_MAX_OUTPUT_SIZE` | `8000` | Tool output truncation limit |\n| `AGENTIC_MAX_STEPS` | `50` | Max agent steps per task |\n| `AGENTIC_MAX_COMPLETION_ATTEMPTS` | `3` | Completion review attempts |\n\n### Configuration Files\n- `.env` - Project-specific (gitignored)\n- `.env.local` - Local overrides\n- `~/.config/agentic-cli/.env` - Global user config\n\n### Provider Examples\n\n**NVIDIA NIM:**\n```bash\nAGENTIC_BASE_URL=https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1\nAGENTIC_API_KEY=your-nvidia-api-key\nAGENTIC_MODEL=z-ai/glm-5.3-flash\n```\n\n**Ollama (local):**\n```bash\nAGENTIC_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1\nAGENTIC_API_KEY=ollama\nAGENTIC_MODEL=llama3.1\n```\n\n**OpenAI:**\n```bash\nAGENTIC_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1\nAGENTIC_API_KEY=sk-...\nAGENTIC_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini\n```\n\n**OpenRouter:**\n```bash\nAGENTIC_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1\nAGENTIC_API_KEY=sk-or-...\nAGENTIC_MODEL=anthropic/claude-3.5-sonnet\n```\n\n---\n\n## Installation & Setup\n\n### Prerequisites\n- Python 3.11+\n- `uv` (recommended) or `pip`\n\n### Installation\n```bash\ncd /Users/glbtech/PycharmProjects/AIAgests/backend\n\n# Using uv (recommended)\nuv sync\n\n# Or using pip\npip install -e .\n```\n\n### Configuration Setup\n```bash\n# Copy example and customize\ncp .env.example .env\n\n# Edit .env with your provider settings\n# Required: AGENTIC_BASE_URL, AGENTIC_API_KEY, AGENTIC_MODEL\n```\n\n### Running\n```bash\n# From backend directory\nuv run python -m src.cli\n\n# Or if installed\nagentic-cli\n```\n\n---\n\n## Testing\n\n### Run Tests\n```bash\nuv run pytest tests/ -v\n```\n\n### Test Coverage\n- **test_agent.py**: Agent loop behavior (empty responses, max tokens, retries, clarification)\n- **test_tools.py**: Tool execution, permissions, path validation, deny list, provider errors\n- **test_completion.py**: Completion reviewer logic\n- **test_interaction_tools.py**: ask_user, plan tool interactions\n\n---\n\n## Security Features\n\n### Path Validation\n- All file operations validated against project root\n- Blocks directory traversal (`../../../etc/passwd`)\n- Uses `os.path.realpath` and `os.path.commonpath` for safety\n\n### Command Deny List\nPrevents dangerous commands:\n- `rm -rf /`, `rm -rf /*`\n- `git push --force`, `git push -f`\n- `dd if=`, `mkfs`, `format `\n- `> /dev/sd`, `chmod -R 777 /`, `chown -R root /`\n\n### Permission Model\n- Write tools require explicit user consent\n- Non-interactive mode: denies write tools by default\n- API keys never logged or stored in chat\n\n---\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\n/Users/glbtech/PycharmProjects/AIAgests/backend/\n├── .agents/\n│   ├── agents/\n│   │   ├── code-reviewer.md\n│   │   └── example-agent.md\n│   └── skills/\n│       ├── example-skill/\n│       │   └── SKILL.md\n│       └── my-new-skill/\n│           └── SKILL.md\n├── agents/\n│   └── agents.md              # Default agent configuration\n├── logs/\n│   └── log.log                # Rotating log file\n├── src/                       # Source code (see Architecture)\n├── tests/                     # Test suite\n├── .env                       # Local config (gitignored)\n├── .env.example               # Config template\n├── CHANGELOG.md               # Version history\n├── package_structure.md       # Package structure doc\n├── projectfile.md             # File listing\n├── pyproject.toml             # Project config & dependencies\n├── README.md                  # User documentation\n├── uv.lock                    # Locked dependencies\n└── SKILL.md                   # Skill template\n```\n\n---\n\n## Development Guidelines\n\n### Code Style\n- **Formatter/Linter**: Ruff (line-length: 100, target: py311)\n- **Type Hints**: Full type annotations\n- **Async**: Use `async/await` throughout\n- **Dataclasses**: Prefer `@dataclass` for data structures\n\n### Adding New Tools\n1. Create `src/tools/new_tool.py` with `ToolSchema` and `Tool` subclass\n2. Add `create_new_tool_tool()` factory function\n3. Register in `cli.py` during initialization\n4. Add tests in `tests/test_tools.py`\n\n### Adding New Providers\n1. Subclass `Provider` in `provider.py`\n2. Implement `complete()` method\n3. Add to CLI initialization logic\n\n---\n\n## Changelog Highlights\n\n| Version | Date | Key Changes |\n|---------|------|-------------|\n| 8d2cdbcd | 2026-11-03 | Initial Agentic CLI with 6 tools, agent loop, permissions, CLI |\n| 22227769 | 2026-11-03 | Added `/permission` slash command |\n| 6e03fbd4 | 2026-11-03 | Reasoning display, interactive permission prompts for ALL tools |\n| dd7a35e5 | 2026-11-04 | Skills & agents support with .md format |\n| 63070a9a | 2026-11-04 | Console script entry, tool output truncation config, fixes |\n| 00059141 | 2026-11-04 | Python 3.10 compatibility (StrEnum fallback) |\n| 00ecc7ac | 2026-11-04 | Non-interactive skill creation |\n| 92e8e591 | 2026-11-06 | Logging system with rotating file handler |\n\n---\n\n## Known Limitations\n\n1. **No streaming support** - Uses non-streaming completions only\n2. **OpenAI-compatible only** - Anthropic/Gemini providers are stubbed\n3. **Single-threaded** - One agent loop at a time\n4. **No persistent memory** - History cleared on `/clear` or restart\n5. **No built-in model management** - Requires external Ollama/NVIDIA/OpenAI\n\n---\n\n## Future Enhancement Ideas\n\n- [ ] Streaming response support\n- [ ] Anthropic/Gemini native providers\n- [ ] Web UI / VS Code extension\n- [ ] Persistent conversation memory (vector DB)\n- [ ] Multi-agent orchestration\n- [ ] Tool result caching\n- [ ] Custom tool plugins via entry points\n- [ ] Telemetry/metrics dashboard\n\n---\n\n## License\n\nMIT License - See LICENSE file for details.\n\n---\n\n*Generated on 2026-11-09*', 'path': 'overview.md'} output=started
2026-11-09 20:26:22 [INFO] agentic_cli: TOOL_CALL: write_file args={'content': '# Agentic CLI - Project Overview\n\n## Project Summary\n\n**Agentic CLI** is a minimal, from-scratch agentic coding tool CLI built in Python. It provides an interactive terminal interface where users can give coding tasks to an AI agent that uses tools to read, search, edit, and run code until the task is completed.\n\n- **Name**: agentic-cli\n- **Version**: 0.1.0\n- **Language**: Python 3.11+\n- **License**: MIT\n- **Repository**: `/Users/glbtech/PycharmProjects/AIAgests/backend`\n\n---\n\n## Purpose & Scope\n\n### Purpose\nCreate a lightweight, provider-agnostic CLI coding agent that:\n- Works with any OpenAI-compatible API (Ollama, OpenAI, OpenRouter, NVIDIA NIM, etc.)\n- Provides a secure, permission-gated tool execution environment\n- Supports extensible skills and agents system\n- Offers transparent reasoning and tool execution visibility\n\n### Scope\n- **In Scope**: Core agent loop, 8 built-in tools, permission system, skills/agents framework, completion verification, logging\n- **Out of Scope**: GUI, web interface, built-in model hosting, non-OpenAI-compatible providers (Anthropic, Gemini - stubbed only)\n\n---\n\n## Architecture\n\n### High-Level Architecture\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                        CLI (src/cli.py)                         │\n│  ┌─────────────┐  ┌─────────────┐  ┌─────────────────────────┐  │\n│  │ Input       │  │ Slash       │  │ Agent Loop              │  │\n│  │ Normalizer  │  │ Commands    │  │ (src/agent.py)          │  │\n│  └──────┬──────┘  └──────┬──────┘  └───────────┬─────────────┘  │\n│         │                │                     │                │\n│         ▼                ▼                     ▼                │\n│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │\n│  │              Tool Registry (src/tools/registry.py)      │   │\n│  │  ┌────────┐ ┌────────┐ ┌────────┐ ┌────────┐ ┌────────┐  │   │\n│  │  │read_   │ │write_  │ │edit_   │ │glob    │ │grep    │  │   │\n│  │  │file    │ │file    │ │file    │ │        │ │        │  │   │\n│  │  └────────┘ └────────┘ └────────┘ └────────┘ └────────┘  │   │\n│  │  ┌────────┐ ┌────────┐ ┌────────┐                          │   │\n│  │  │bash    │ │ask_    │ │plan    │                          │   │\n│  │  │        │ │user    │ │        │                          │   │\n│  │  └────────┘ └────────┘ └────────┘                          │   │\n│  └────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┘   │\n│                           │                                       │\n│         ┌─────────────────┼─────────────────┐                    │\n│         ▼                 ▼                 ▼                    │\n│  ┌────────────┐   ┌────────────┐   ┌────────────┐               │\n│  │ Permission │   │  Provider  │   │  Logger    │               │\n│  │ Gate       │   │  Adapter   │   │  (logs/)   │               │\n│  └────────────┘   └────────────┘   └────────────┘               │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### Module Structure\n\n```\nsrc/\n├── __init__.py              # Package initialization\n├── agent.py                 # Agent loop with max steps, loop detection, output limit handling\n├── agents.py                # Agent loader (individual .md files + agents.md)\n├── cli.py                   # REPL with slash commands, rich console UI\n├── completion.py            # Completion reviewer (verifies task completion)\n├── config.py                # Configuration from env/file (.env support)\n├── logger.py                # Rotating file logging (logs/log.log)\n├── permissions.py           # Path validation, deny list, permission gate\n├── provider.py              # OpenAI-compatible provider adapter\n├── skills.py                # Skill loader (.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md)\n├── system_prompt.py         # System prompt builder + AGENT.md loader\n├── types.py                 # Internal message format (provider-independent)\n└── tools/\n    ├── __init__.py          # Tool exports\n    ├── registry.py          # Tool registry\n    ├── read_file.py         # Read file with offset/limit\n    ├── write_file.py        # Write file (creates dirs, overwrites)\n    ├── edit_file.py         # Edit file by exact string replacement\n    ├── glob_tool.py         # Find files matching glob pattern\n    ├── grep_tool.py         # Regex search in files\n    ├── bash_tool.py         # Execute shell commands\n    ├── ask_tool.py          # Ask user questions (with options)\n    └── plan_tool.py         # Present plans for approval\n```\n\n---\n\n## Key Features\n\n### 1. Provider-Agnostic LLM Integration\n- Works with any OpenAI-compatible API endpoint\n- Tested with: NVIDIA NIM, Ollama, OpenAI, OpenRouter\n- Configurable via environment variables or `.env` file\n- Supports reasoning models (qwen3.5, deepseek-r1, etc.)\n\n### 2. 8 Built-in Tools\n| Tool | Category | Permission | Description |\n|------|----------|------------|-------------|\n| `read_file` | Read | Auto | Read file with optional offset/limit |\n| `write_file` | Write | Prompt | Write content, creates parent dirs |\n| `edit_file` | Write | Prompt | Exact string replacement (unique match required) |\n| `glob` | Read | Auto | Find files matching glob pattern |\n| `grep` | Read | Auto | Regex search in files |\n| `bash` | Write | Prompt | Execute shell commands (with deny list) |\n| `ask_user` | Interactive | Auto | Ask user questions with optional choices |\n| `plan` | Interactive | Auto | Present implementation plans for approval |\n\n### 3. Permission System\n- **Auto-allowed**: `read_file`, `glob`, `grep` (run automatically)\n- **Prompt required**: `write_file`, `edit_file`, `bash` (ask each time)\n- **Interactive options**: `y` (allow once), `a` (always allow), `u` (auto-allow), `n` (deny), `d` (deny always)\n- **Pre-configuration**: `/permission allow <tool> [always|auto]`\n- **Security**: Path validation (blocks outside project root), command deny list\n\n### 4. Agent Loop\n- Maximum steps per task (default: 50, configurable)\n- Loop detection (stops on repeated identical tool calls)\n- Output token limit handling with automatic continuation\n- Empty response retry with clarification callback\n- Context window utilization logging\n\n### 5. Completion Verification\n- Automatic review after agent claims completion\n- Uses separate LLM call to verify task fulfillment\n- Up to 3 attempts (configurable) with feedback loop\n- Returns detailed findings if incomplete\n\n### 6. Skills & Agents System\n- **Skills**: `.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` with YAML frontmatter\n- **Agents**: `.agents/agents/<name>.md` or `agents/agents.md`\n- Auto-discovered and loaded at startup\n- Included in system prompt for agent awareness\n- CLI commands: `/skills`, `/agents` for management\n\n### 7. Slash Commands\n| Command | Description |\n|---------|-------------|\n| `/help` | Show help |\n| `/clear` | Clear conversation history & permissions |\n| `/model [name]` | Show or change model |\n| `/permission [list|allow|deny|reset]` | Manage tool permissions |\n| `/skills [list|show|create]` | Manage skills |\n| `/agents [list|show|create]` | Manage agents |\n| `/exit` | Exit the CLI |\n\n### 8. Logging System\n- Rotating file handler (10MB, 5 backups) at `logs/log.log`\n- Logs: commands, permissions, tool calls, reasoning, errors\n- Console shows warnings/errors only\n\n### 9. Input Normalization\n- Normalizes user input to English objective + actionable tasks\n- Corrects spelling/grammar, preserves intent\n- Uses separate lightweight agent loop\n\n---\n\n## Dependencies\n\n### Runtime Dependencies (from `pyproject.toml`)\n| Package | Version | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|---------|\n| `httpx` | >=0.27 | Async HTTP client for LLM API calls |\n| `pydantic` | >=2.8 | Data validation (used in types) |\n| `python-dotenv` | >=1.0 | Load `.env` configuration files |\n| `rich` | >=13.7 | Terminal UI (panels, tables, markdown) |\n| `pyyaml` | >=6.0 | Parse YAML frontmatter in skills/agents |\n\n### Development Dependencies\n| Package | Version | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|---------|\n| `pytest` | >=8.2 | Test framework |\n| `pytest-asyncio` | >=0.23 | Async test support |\n| `ruff` | >=0.5 | Linting/formatting |\n\n### Python Version\n- **Requires**: Python >= 3.11\n- **StrEnum fallback** for Python 3.10 compatibility\n\n---\n\n## Configuration\n\n### Environment Variables\n| Variable | Default | Description |\n|----------|---------|-------------|\n| `AGENTIC_BASE_URL` | `http://localhost:11434/v1` | OpenAI-compatible API endpoint |\n| `AGENTIC_API_KEY` | `ollama` | Provider API key |\n| `AGENTIC_MODEL` | `llama3.1` | Model name |\n| `AGENTIC_PROJECT_ROOT` | `.` | Project directory |\n| `AGENTIC_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` | `300` | Model request timeout |\n| `AGENTIC_MAX_COMPLETION_TOKENS` | `8192` | Max generated tokens per response |\n| `AGENTIC_CONTEXT_WINDOW_TOKENS` | `32768` | Context budget for token tracking |\n| `AGENTIC_MAX_OUTPUT_SIZE` | `8000` | Tool output truncation limit |\n| `AGENTIC_MAX_STEPS` | `50` | Max agent steps per task |\n| `AGENTIC_MAX_COMPLETION_ATTEMPTS` | `3` | Completion review attempts |\n\n### Configuration Files\n- `.env` - Project-specific (gitignored)\n- `.env.local` - Local overrides\n- `~/.config/agentic-cli/.env` - Global user config\n\n### Provider Examples\n\n**NVIDIA NIM:**\n```bash\nAGENTIC_BASE_URL=https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1\nAGENTIC_API_KEY=your-nvidia-api-key\nAGENTIC_MODEL=z-ai/glm-5.3-flash\n```\n\n**Ollama (local):**\n```bash\nAGENTIC_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1\nAGENTIC_API_KEY=ollama\nAGENTIC_MODEL=llama3.1\n```\n\n**OpenAI:**\n```bash\nAGENTIC_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1\nAGENTIC_API_KEY=sk-...\nAGENTIC_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini\n```\n\n**OpenRouter:**\n```bash\nAGENTIC_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1\nAGENTIC_API_KEY=sk-or-...\nAGENTIC_MODEL=anthropic/claude-3.5-sonnet\n```\n\n---\n\n## Installation & Setup\n\n### Prerequisites\n- Python 3.11+\n- `uv` (recommended) or `pip`\n\n### Installation\n```bash\ncd /Users/glbtech/PycharmProjects/AIAgests/backend\n\n# Using uv (recommended)\nuv sync\n\n# Or using pip\npip install -e .\n```\n\n### Configuration Setup\n```bash\n# Copy example and customize\ncp .env.example .env\n\n# Edit .env with your provider settings\n# Required: AGENTIC_BASE_URL, AGENTIC_API_KEY, AGENTIC_MODEL\n```\n\n### Running\n```bash\n# From backend directory\nuv run python -m src.cli\n\n# Or if installed\nagentic-cli\n```\n\n---\n\n## Testing\n\n### Run Tests\n```bash\nuv run pytest tests/ -v\n```\n\n### Test Coverage\n- **test_agent.py**: Agent loop behavior (empty responses, max tokens, retries, clarification)\n- **test_tools.py**: Tool execution, permissions, path validation, deny list, provider errors\n- **test_completion.py**: Completion reviewer logic\n- **test_interaction_tools.py**: ask_user, plan tool interactions\n\n---\n\n## Security Features\n\n### Path Validation\n- All file operations validated against project root\n- Blocks directory traversal (`../../../etc/passwd`)\n- Uses `os.path.realpath` and `os.path.commonpath` for safety\n\n### Command Deny List\nPrevents dangerous commands:\n- `rm -rf /`, `rm -rf /*`\n- `git push --force`, `git push -f`\n- `dd if=`, `mkfs`, `format `\n- `> /dev/sd`, `chmod -R 777 /`, `chown -R root /`\n\n### Permission Model\n- Write tools require explicit user consent\n- Non-interactive mode: denies write tools by default\n- API keys never logged or stored in chat\n\n---\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\n/Users/glbtech/PycharmProjects/AIAgests/backend/\n├── .agents/\n│   ├── agents/\n│   │   ├── code-reviewer.md\n│   │   └── example-agent.md\n│   └── skills/\n│       ├── example-skill/\n│       │   └── SKILL.md\n│       └── my-new-skill/\n│           └── SKILL.md\n├── agents/\n│   └── agents.md              # Default agent configuration\n├── logs/\n│   └── log.log                # Rotating log file\n├── src/                       # Source code (see Architecture)\n├── tests/                     # Test suite\n├── .env                       # Local config (gitignored)\n├── .env.example               # Config template\n├── CHANGELOG.md               # Version history\n├── package_structure.md       # Package structure doc\n├── projectfile.md             # File listing\n├── pyproject.toml             # Project config & dependencies\n├── README.md                  # User documentation\n├── uv.lock                    # Locked dependencies\n└── SKILL.md                   # Skill template\n```\n\n---\n\n## Development Guidelines\n\n### Code Style\n- **Formatter/Linter**: Ruff (line-length: 100, target: py311)\n- **Type Hints**: Full type annotations\n- **Async**: Use `async/await` throughout\n- **Dataclasses**: Prefer `@dataclass` for data structures\n\n### Adding New Tools\n1. Create `src/tools/new_tool.py` with `ToolSchema` and `Tool` subclass\n2. Add `create_new_tool_tool()` factory function\n3. Register in `cli.py` during initialization\n4. Add tests in `tests/test_tools.py`\n\n### Adding New Providers\n1. Subclass `Provider` in `provider.py`\n2. Implement `complete()` method\n3. Add to CLI initialization logic\n\n---\n\n## Changelog Highlights\n\n| Version | Date | Key Changes |\n|---------|------|-------------|\n| 8d2cdbcd | 2026-11-03 | Initial Agentic CLI with 6 tools, agent loop, permissions, CLI |\n| 22227769 | 2026-11-03 | Added `/permission` slash command |\n| 6e03fbd4 | 2026-11-03 | Reasoning display, interactive permission prompts for ALL tools |\n| dd7a35e5 | 2026-11-04 | Skills & agents support with .md format |\n| 63070a9a | 2026-11-04 | Console script entry, tool output truncation config, fixes |\n| 00059141 | 2026-11-04 | Python 3.10 compatibility (StrEnum fallback) |\n| 00ecc7ac | 2026-11-04 | Non-interactive skill creation |\n| 92e8e591 | 2026-11-06 | Logging system with rotating file handler |\n\n---\n\n## Known Limitations\n\n1. **No streaming support** - Uses non-streaming completions only\n2. **OpenAI-compatible only** - Anthropic/Gemini providers are stubbed\n3. **Single-threaded** - One agent loop at a time\n4. **No persistent memory** - History cleared on `/clear` or restart\n5. **No built-in model management** - Requires external Ollama/NVIDIA/OpenAI\n\n---\n\n## Future Enhancement Ideas\n\n- [ ] Streaming response support\n- [ ] Anthropic/Gemini native providers\n- [ ] Web UI / VS Code extension\n- [ ] Persistent conversation memory (vector DB)\n- [ ] Multi-agent orchestration\n- [ ] Tool result caching\n- [ ] Custom tool plugins via entry points\n- [ ] Telemetry/metrics dashboard\n\n---\n\n## License\n\nMIT License - See LICENSE file for details.\n\n---\n\n*Generated on 2026-11-09*', 'path': 'overview.md'} output=Written 14337 chars to overview.md
